Package: slice
Title: Sparse + Low-Rank Inverse Covariance Estimation (SLICE)
Version: 0.0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Martin", "Ondrus", email = "mondrus@ualberta.ca", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Author: Martin Ondrus [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Martin Ondrus <mondrus@ualberta.ca>
Description: The SLICE package implements efficient estimation of joint sparse and low‐rank inverse covariance (precision) matrices for latent-variable Gaussian graphical models. The main routine includes a pseudo-EM algorithm with a simple convex regularizer that simultaneously recovers a sparse precision matrix and low-rank latent structure. Users can flexibly choose among multiple sparse penalties (e.g., LASSO, SCAD) and estimation schemes (e.g, CLIME), and perform model selection via cross-validation, all of which are implemented in the main methods.
